Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

Let's denote the number of students in class $5A$ as $x$. According to the problem, we can set up an equation as follows:

\begin{align*}
23(x-23) &= 13(x-13)\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 23x-23^2 &= 13x-13^2\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 23x-23^2-13x+13^2 &= 0\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 10x-23^2+13^2 &= 0\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 10x-23^2+13^2 &= 0\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 10x-529+169 &= 0\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 1
