[Step 780] Q: Gino has 15 brown bears, 24 white bears, and some black bears. Gino has 66 bears. How many black bears does Gino have?
Ground truth: 27
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

To find out how many black bears Gino has, we need to subtract the number of brown and white bears from the total number of bears.

Total number of bears = 66
Number of brown bears = 15
Number of white bears = 24

Number of black bears = Total number of bears - Number of brown bears - Number of white bears
= 66 - 15 - 24
= 66 - 39
= 27

So, Gino has 27 black bears.

