[Step 860] Q: I have 150 pieces of cake. There are some friends in my house. I would like to give each friend the same amount of cake, which is 3 pieces per friend. How many friends are in my house?
Ground truth: 50
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>

To find the number of friends in your house, we need to divide the total amount of cake by the amount of cake each friend should get.

Total cake = 150 pieces
Cake per friend = 3 pieces

Number of friends = Total cake / Cake per friend
= 150 / 3
= 50

Since you can't have a fraction of a friend, this means you have 50 friends in your house.

<end_working_out>

<SOLUTION>50</SO
